            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_aba5d702078aed2aa34748dd",
            "source_text": "The word2vec tool contains two models, namely *skip-gram* :cite:`Mikolov.Sutskever.Chen.ea.2013`  and *continuous bag of words* (CBOW) :cite:`Mikolov.Chen.Corrado.ea.2013`.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining_word2vec_b032",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining",
            "content_sha256": "663bbb2ae916c03cff8c654c5a63a15340ba7a1e62b0bba5d19bfa32de69f17b",
            "context_id": "ctx_3e4d253c9ff11b6a3080d990",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "POSITIVE_DEFINITION_PROPOSAL",
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "continuous bag of words",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_33191bdfdb87b3833c84d23d",
            "source_text": "For example,\nin the same text sequence \"the\", \"man\", \"loves\", \"his\", and \"son\", with \"loves\" as the center word and the context window size being 2,\nthe continuous bag of words model\nconsiders\nthe conditional probability of generating the center word \"loves\" based on the context words \"the\", \"man\", \"his\" and \"son\" (as shown in :numref:`fig_cbow`), which is",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining_word2vec_b035",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining",
            "content_sha256": "f57c87a721200739f29210ce52ba09d4eba123c42b3522057642be23af46903d",
            "context_id": "ctx_500e392a6212984ed97679b6",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "continuous bag of words",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_18d32bd5e9e5e76b2e7a59e4",
            "source_text": "Since there are multiple context words\nin the continuous bag of words model,\nthese context word vectors are averaged\nin the calculation of the conditional probability.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining_word2vec_b032",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining",
            "content_sha256": "d520a84526c732a100d01121a20c9691e75b37a22fc9bc41ea4828d46b2e0aa3",
            "context_id": "ctx_7592d6eb1986a0c2bd965c36",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "POSITIVE_DEFINITION_PROPOSAL",
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "continuous bag of words",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_d817077031ebd0ab4c570d0a",
            "source_text": "The major difference\nfrom the skip-gram model is that\nthe continuous bag of words model\nassumes that a center word is generated\nbased on its surrounding context words in the text sequence.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining_word2vec_b009",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining",
            "content_sha256": "02351ac6beccf6972aba3fd938662b5ac96f62c6051c924657781c068418345d",
            "context_id": "ctx_8ae5ddde35de799cd4b51696",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "BACKUP"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "continuous bag of words",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_120717dab0f18c821c479676",
            "source_text": "Since supervision comes from the data without labels,\nboth skip-gram and continuous bag of words\nare self-supervised models.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining_word2vec_b032",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining",
            "content_sha256": "905940cbe5460a9cce711ab6ee4775d282f5302fd6accd53afab4129ffb15ebe",
            "context_id": "ctx_9539bbe8c2ac486d267b808a",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "BACKUP"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "continuous bag of words",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_8cf77efb03581702fc05aa42",
            "source_text": "The *continuous bag of words* (CBOW) model is similar to the skip-gram model.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining_word2vec_b034",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining",
